2. Conformal negative energy (torus Casimir class, n = 4)
   |ρ_Cas|(L =  1.0 Gpc) ≈ 1.83e-130 eV⁴  →  |ρ_Cas|/ρ_rad,0 = 5.6e-116
   |ρ_Cas|(L = 14.0 Gpc) ≈ 4.77e-135 eV⁴  →  |ρ_Cas|/ρ_rad,0 = 1.5e-120
   Same a⁻⁴ scaling as radiation ⟹ the ratio is FROZEN at today's
   value forever. A future crossing needs the radiation sector
   net-negative NOW — excluded by N_eff ≈ 3. Dead twice over:
   measured sign, and ~119 orders of magnitude.

3. Ghost-condensate transient (negative stiff excursion, n = 6)
   The recorded arrow sector sits on its stable attractor at the
   dark-energy scale. The exotic-fluid target needs |ρ_X| at the
   handover budget — `scripts/bounce_rp_required_X.py` prices the
   shortfall at 10¹⁹–10³² depending on the handover variant, and the
