5. Attractive interaction energy at high density
   The recorded medium quartic is repulsive (λ > 0, c_s² > 0 — the
   floor exists because of it); the portal couplings are perturbative
   and tiny. No recorded channel turns the interaction energy
   negative at crunch density. Window: FAIL — no candidate exists.

VERDICT — M5 CLOSES NEGATIVE
  No component of the recorded theory can be the exotic fluid: every
  negative-energy corner fails on measured sign (frozen ratio), on
  budget (19–119 orders), or on nonexistence. The exotic-fluid branch
  is UNBUILDABLE from native parts.

  Consequences for the reconstruction:
